          "text": "Created the crate and demonstrated the pattern using `std::sync::LazyLock` in `src/main.rs:3`:\n\n```rust\nstatic CONFIG: LazyLock<String> = LazyLock::new(|| {\n    let value = std::env::var(\"APP_ENV\").unwrap_or_else(|_| \"development\".to_string());\n    format!(\"running in {value}\")\n});\n```\n\n`LazyLock` (stable since Rust 1.80) runs initialization once on first access and is thread-safe. Use `OnceLock<T>` instead if you need to set the value with runtime arguments or fallible logic later via `.set()`/`.get_or_init()`. Run with `cargo run`.",
